/[0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f]*.gif

# Session-scoped audit evidence at repo root (regenerated per audit cycle)
/audit-results.md

# Local Claude Code settings (never commit)
.claude/settings.local.json

# Project-root context files, at repo root only (this is a public fork).
# /blog brand and /blog discourse write these to the project root, so running
# them with this repository as the working directory drops them here, where a
# `git add -A` sweeps them in without asking. They hold positioning,
# competitive read and voice of customer: the material a public repository is
# the worst place for. Anchored to the root so a template or reference
# carrying the same basename inside skills/ stays tracked.
/BRAND.md
/VOICE.md
/DISCOURSE.md

# Calibration corpus: third-party article bodies pulled for readability
# calibration. Bulky, and republishing someone else's text from a public
# repository is not a fight worth having.
/corpus/
